// R_ONE           MAYBE. ONE is the bound junction's coupled whole (R244 L19–L23; CARRIER). Its identity and incidence are
//                 bound; what it cannot absorb is MAYBE (R243 L16); its stability and enough-for-fold are not yet read on it.
// R_MANY          MAYBE. The four whole ▽ roots per junction are identified: 120 positions over 30 junctions, each unique
//                 (R243 L12, L18). As the MANY of one identified FPP product: MAYBE (R243 L15).
// R_ADMISSION     MAYBE. No record reads FPP's internal MUST against the tick's admission.
// R_FOLDABLE_ONES SAME within scope: four-part quotient families on links 6→7 and 7→8, each counted once by ancestry
//                 (5,120 families at 6→7, 20,480 at 7→8, and through both refinements: R155 L13–L16, L20); the
//                 centre-of-centre ▽ return is witnessed for 2,720 families with all 8,160 root-G cases carried separately
//                 (R155 L18). The open operand FPP_PRODUCT_FOLDABLE_ONE_MEMBERSHIP_AND_Q1_CONTRIBUTION is narrowed,
//                 not removed. Scope: refinement families; not transferred to the junction product. On the junction
//                 product: MAYBE (R243 L15).
// R_POLARITY      SAME within scope: each member's identity and inherited junction membership in the bound dual-machine
//                 junction (R195 L8–L18) reads THIS → THIS (domain members) and NO → NO (witness members) on both links;
//                 no NOT_SAME member, over all 30 junctions with root-G cases separate (R199 L8–L16). Refinement creates new incidence; that new
//                 incidence is not covered (R201 L25). Scope: the junction's domain and witness members, not its four ▽ roots.
//                 On the junction product: MAYBE (the four ▽ roots' q₂ is not read).
// R_DELTA         MAYBE. Retained: no identity-bound shed found in the inspected records of link 7→8 (R098 L9–L11). Its
//                 joint NO (R098 L11–L13) is superseded: absence in records does not falsify constitutive shedding; the
//                 witness is the substrate unfolding, not yet bound (DSUB L12–L21).
// R_ARITY         MAYBE. The bound junction 2 × 2 supplies a four that is not a refinement four (R195 L13–L27); this
//                 correspondence now reads the coupled four on the junction. Its stability is not read; the closed six-fan at
//                 the junction midpoint (four ▽ roots + two △) is an untested candidate (R243 L22–L23, L33–L35).
// R_DIRECTION     MAYBE. First sentence decided by Devon ("yes", D202 L6) on Claude's proposal (D202 L10–L12), witnessed as
//                 the recursion (R238 L22–L23); its ONE → four shape is D202's (D202 L11). Second sentence, proposed in v0.1.19 on R243 L27–L32 (V0119 L350), was decided by Devon at the promotion of v0.1.19 (RV0119 L26–L29); it replaces D202's
//                 "corresponds to the MANY children → ONE parent relation". The first sentence's rewording to whole / parts in this successor (R258) is Devon's to decide at promotion.

